    if (row.kind === "sequenced") this.rows.set(key, { kind: "cached", value: row.value });
    this.changed(key);

dsh-projection-persist README · Where reconnects come from (a different chain — not this plugin's job)：1. The renderer-side `third_party/blink/renderer/modules/websockets/websocket_channel_impl.cc` has **no ping/pong handling at all**;
   it only receives data frames over a Mojo data pipe (`ApplyBackpressure` / `RemoveBackpressure`).
2. The code that answers a ping with a pong lives in `net/websockets/websocket_channel.cc:766-772` (`case kOpCodePing:` -> `SendFrameInternal(... kOpCodePong ...)`),
   inside the network service `services/network/websocket.cc`.
3. Every WebView2 instance runs its own `network.mojom.NetworkService` utility process, separate from the renderer;
   the renderer itself holds **no** TCP connection.
